# {{ project_name }}

Product brief, roadmap and glossary: `docs/brief.md`. Decisions: `docs/adr/`. Feature specs and
tasks: `docs/specs/`.

- The HTTP contract in `contract/` is the source of truth. Change it first, run `just generate`,
  then implement. Never edit generated code (`packages/api-client/src/generated`,
  `apps/api` generated files).
- Mobile is offline-first: synced entities use client-generated UUIDv7 ids, a server `version`
  and soft deletes (see the sync ADR).
- Done means `just verify` passes. Hooks run `just check-file` after edits, `just test-affected`
  when a task is completed and `just verify` before the session ends.
- Every task ends in a pull request titled `[NNNN-MM] <title>` with a `risk:*` label; never push
  to `main`.
- Agents commit as `{{ agent_name }}` (`just agent-identity <model> <task>` in their worktree,
  which adds `Agent-Model` / `Agent-Task` trailers); humans commit as themselves. PRs merge
  with a merge commit, never squash or rebase, so `git blame` keeps the two apart.
- Feature work runs through the pscaffold skills: `spec` → `plan` → `orchestrate`. Tasks are
  implemented by the `implementer` agent (`.claude/agents/`), one worktree and one PR each.
